    "created_at": "2025-11-21T01:08:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-21T01:08:23Z",
    "body": "Is it not possible to have scoped registry for both document and shadow like described in the table?\n```\n  const documentRegistry = new CustomElementRegistry();\n  const contentDocument = document.implementation.createHTMLDocument();\n  documentRegistry.initialize(contentDocument);\n  const element = document.createElement('div');\n\n  const shadowRegistry = new CustomElementRegistry();\n  const elementShadow = element.attachShadow({ mode: \"closed\", customElementRegistry: shadowRegistry });\n```\n\nThis will give us a scenario where both document and shadow is using a scoped registry. I'm guessing we'd want to append `shadowrootcustomelementregistry` in the serialization if the two scoped registries used by document and shadow are different, do not append if they're the same, right?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
