    "created_at": "2025-11-21T06:27:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-21T06:27:00Z",
    "body": "I'm very confused by @sorvell's comment above. A prime reason to have `shadowrootcustomelementregistry` is for scoped registries. Scoped registries not getting that when serialized means that when they get parsed again they could end up in the global registry.\n\n@ja-y-son I think even when they are the same you probably want to add it as initialization doesn't cross the node tree boundary. So the shadow root might attain the wrong registry when it gets attached the next time around if it doesn't have the attribute.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
