    "created_at": "2025-11-21T14:31:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-21T14:31:45Z",
    "body": "> I'm very confused by @sorvell's comment above. A prime reason to have shadowrootcustomelementregistry is for scoped registries\n\nI'm sorry, I was mixed up. That makes sense, I wasn't following the table. \n\nDoes this match your understanding? It should match https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11892#issuecomment-3556460240 except where noted.\n\n### Append shadowrootcustomelementregistry? \n\nyes ✅, no ❌\n\n|  | document is null                           | document is scoped                 | document is global                           |\n|------------------------|--------------------------------|------------------------|----------------------------------|\n| shadow is null                   | ❌ (see https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11892#issuecomment-3558274360) | ✅ **  | ✅  |\n| shadow is scoped                 | ✅ | ✅ (see https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11892#issuecomment-3561595685)  |✅ |\n| shadow is global                 | N/A            | N/A   | ❌                                |\n\n** case\n\n```js\nconst documentRegistry = new CustomElementRegistry();\nconst contentDocument = document.implementation.createHTMLDocument();\ndocumentRegistry.initialize(contentDocument);\nconst element = contentDocument.createElement('div');\nconst elementShadow = element.attachShadow({ mode: \"closed\", serializable: true, customElementRegistry: null });\nconsole.assert(element.getHTML({serializableShadowRoots} === \n  `<div><template shadowrootmode=\"closed\" shadowrootserializable shadowrootcustomelementregistry></template></div>`);\n```",
